# AshReXcue settings. Edit only if you know what each value does.
# Prefer the WebUI Settings tab or the action menu: both validate ranges and rewrite this file safely.
# A malformed line or an out-of-range value is replaced with its default on next boot.
# Do not experiment with out-of-bounds values. If you break it, that's on you.

# Mode Guidelines
# Protection action on loop detection.
# 1 = disable culprit modules only (safest).
# 2 = disable culprits + reboot to recovery (nuclear).
# Allowed: 1, 2. Anything else is fixed to 1.

# Threshold Guidelines
# Consecutive failed boots before action.
# Allowed: 1, 2, 3, 4. Anything else is fixed to 2.
# Set by the installer or the WebUI. Do not set to "none".

# Loops Guidelines
# Boot loop counter. Managed by the module, do not edit.
# Max allowed: 10. Anything higher is impossible and reset to 0.

# Disable Guidelines
# Current protection state. Managed by the module, do not edit.
# none = no action yet, partial = culprits disabled, full = lockdown active.
# Any other value is unexpected and reset to none.

# Timeout Guidelines
# Seconds to wait for boot completion before triggering protection.
# Allowed range: 1-100. Anything outside is fixed to 60.

# Stability Time Guidelines
# Seconds the watchdog watches the framework after boot.
# Allowed range: 45-90. Anything outside is fixed to 60.
# Lower = faster rescue, more false positives on slow devices.
# Higher = more tolerant, slower to catch a real post-boot loop.

# Log Guidelines
# Log session counter. Managed by the module, do not edit.

# Install Date Guidelines
# Install date. Managed by the module, do not edit.

# Boot Markers Guidelines
# Boot state markers. Managed by the module, do not edit.

# Extra Stability Guidelines
# Watch servicemanager and vold by PID in addition to the core framework.
# Allowed: On, Off. Anything else is fixed to Off.
# Monitor Scripts Guidelines
# Track service.d scripts alongside modules.
# Note: post-mount.d and post-fs-data.d scripts are visible in the WebUI for manual
# management, but cannot be caught automatically if they cause a bootloop, as they
# run before this module's own boot scripts execute.
# Allowed: On, Off. Anything else is fixed to Off.

# Whitelist Guidelines
# Comma-separated list of modules/scripts never disabled. Always contains AshLooper.
# Format: "AshLooper,other.module,svc:script.sh".
# Do not edit by hand, use the WebUI Whitelist tab or the action menu.

# Props
mode=none
threshold=none
loops=0
disable=none
timeout=60
stability_time=60
log=1-0
install_date=none
boot=none
boot_id=none
kernel_uptime=none
extra_stability=Off
monitor_scripts=Off
whitelist="AshLooper"
